    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123-a3">

                <pb facs="0307" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg235"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 349.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Tinsly</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 21,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: You will please see without delay John
                    McInerny and Patrick Slattery, suspects claiming to be American citizens and
                    confined in Limerick jail, and say to each <pb facs="0308" n="236"
                        xml:id="pg236"/> of them that “in case he should be liberated you have
                    authority to pay him forty pounds sterling for his passage to the United States”
                    for which sum you may draw upon me at sight.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
